Repost goldens (TestRepostGolden). Annotate, Overflow and Header are
synthetic; nothing here is any bot's wording.

One section per case:

  -- <name> --
  opt <key>[=<value>] ...       options, any number of opt lines:
                                  wrap=angle|none, nospoiler, maxlen=N,
                                  maxbodies=N, unexamined=N, header=<string>
  change <string> [spoiler]     one Change, in order: Result.URL and Link.URL
                                are the string, Result.Changed is true
  full <required> <string>...   Annotate(c, false) for the preceding change
  compact <required> <string>...
                                Annotate(c, true) for the preceding change
  overflow <string>             Overflow is set: the string with {o} and {u}
                                replaced by the omitted and unexamined counts
  overflow-at <omitted> <string>
                                Overflow's line for that omitted count instead
                                (an empty string included)
  body <string>                 one expected body, in order
  nobodies                      Repost returns nil
  calls <change> <full> <compact>
                                expected Annotate call counts for change
                                number <change> (0-based)

Annotate is nil unless a case has a full or compact line; a change without
one returns (nil, 0) for that mode. <required> may be any integer (Repost
clamps it). <string> is as in find.txtar ("x"*N repeats, " + " joins), and
each <string>... is zero or more strings separated by spaces. Blank lines and
lines starting with "# " are ignored.
